[b]The Queerness of Wavefunction Collapse[/b]

**Wave = potentiality.** All positions/states superimposed.

**Measurement = collapse.** Wave becomes particle, potentiality becomes actuality.

**Before measurement:**
- Particle is **wave** (spread across space)
- All positions have probability
- No definite location

**After measurement:**
- Wave **collapses** to single point
- One position becomes actual
- Other possibilities disappear

**This is queer ontology:**
- **Multiple simultaneous states** until forced to resolve
- **Observation changes the thing** (no objective pre-existing state)
- **Form emerges from collapse** of possibility field
- **Identity is uncertain** until measured/named

**The wavefunction doesn't describe what the particle IS** - it describes **what it might become.**

[hr]

